WEBVTT

00:00:02.890 --> 00:00:08.570
At long last, today's the final selection! I wanted to get there early and prepare, but...

00:00:08.860 --> 00:00:11.820
I can't believe I overslept!

00:00:26.250 --> 00:00:28.630
Y-Yunoki-sempai?

00:00:28.880 --> 00:00:32.510
You've got such a stupid look on your face already this morning, Hino.

00:00:32.840 --> 00:00:35.620
Yunoki-sempai, why are you here?

00:00:35.620 --> 00:00:39.930
It's because I'm participating in the final selection, obviously.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:43.840
But, didn't you go to England?

00:00:43.840 --> 00:00:47.400
I went in order to go through the proceedings to cancel the study abroad.

00:00:48.640 --> 00:00:51.780
So you didn't really go to study abroad?

00:00:52.900 --> 00:00:55.540
Don't blame me you were so easily fooled.

00:00:55.540 --> 00:00:58.360
He's just so...

00:00:59.570 --> 00:01:01.330
Same as ever, I guess.

00:01:01.670 --> 00:01:04.090
What? You're acting weird.

00:01:04.090 --> 00:01:06.570
Ah, never mind.

00:01:07.440 --> 00:01:13.000
Um, I'm looking forward to your performance, Yunoki-sempai.

00:01:13.000 --> 00:01:15.880
Just as annoying as ever, I see.

00:01:17.860 --> 00:01:23.210
Thank goodness. We can do the final selection with everyone together!

00:01:36.690 --> 00:01:40.070
My Beloved Ave Maria.

00:01:44.340 --> 00:01:45.550
Yunoki-sama!

00:01:45.550 --> 00:01:47.790
Is he real? Is this not a dream?

00:01:48.060 --> 00:01:50.810
Welcome back!

00:01:50.810 --> 00:01:52.130
Yunoki-sempai!

00:01:52.420 --> 00:01:56.380
My, please don't look at me like I'm some ghost.

00:01:56.380 --> 00:01:58.710
You came back, Yunoki!

00:01:58.710 --> 00:02:00.100
But, why?

00:02:00.100 --> 00:02:04.470
Yunoki went to England in order to cancel his studying abroad.

00:02:04.750 --> 00:02:06.680
To cancel it?

00:02:06.680 --> 00:02:08.790
Kanayan, you knew?

00:02:08.790 --> 00:02:11.250
Well, I am his homeroom teacher.

00:02:11.250 --> 00:02:14.070
Then why didn't you tell us?!

00:02:14.730 --> 00:02:17.120
Just a little production.

00:02:17.120 --> 00:02:18.860
This way everyone is more excited, right?

00:02:20.710 --> 00:02:23.660
Sorry about surprising everyone.

00:02:23.970 --> 00:02:26.420
It's fine, don't worry about it.

00:02:26.420 --> 00:02:29.490
It's definitely more interesting when there are more rivals.

00:02:29.490 --> 00:02:32.880
But I'm really happy! Let's all do our best!

00:02:33.150 --> 00:02:35.010
Of course, Hihara.

00:02:35.460 --> 00:02:38.300
Tsukimori-kun and Shimizu-kun as well.

00:02:38.570 --> 00:02:40.810
Yes, same to you.

00:02:40.810 --> 00:02:42.570
Welcome back.

00:02:51.140 --> 00:02:52.790
I made it.

00:02:55.700 --> 00:02:58.070
It's finally time, Kahoko Hino.

00:03:00.470 --> 00:03:01.550
Lili.

00:03:01.550 --> 00:03:03.620
You really worked hard for today.

00:03:03.850 --> 00:03:07.980
Perform with all your heart so that you have no regrets.

00:03:07.980 --> 00:03:10.540
Yes. I'll do my best!

00:03:10.740 --> 00:03:14.170
And for that, I'll give you the best dress!

00:03:14.170 --> 00:03:15.960
Um, about that...

00:03:16.290 --> 00:03:17.300
Hino-sempai!

00:03:18.190 --> 00:03:19.630
Nozaki-san?

00:03:20.040 --> 00:03:21.090
Um, this is...

00:03:21.090 --> 00:03:24.090
This is no time for dancing, you have a big problem!

00:03:29.030 --> 00:03:32.080
I'm sorry, Hino-san.

00:03:32.080 --> 00:03:35.150
Mori-san, what happened?

00:03:35.150 --> 00:03:39.310
My bicycle got hit and I fell down...

00:03:39.310 --> 00:03:41.640
It wasn't Mori-san's fault!

00:03:41.640 --> 00:03:45.790
I saw it, that guy was driving really crazy!

00:03:45.790 --> 00:03:47.800
I'm really sorry!

00:03:47.800 --> 00:03:51.580
I wanted to play your accompaniment until the very end...

00:03:53.070 --> 00:03:55.310
I'll be your accompanist instead.

00:03:55.950 --> 00:04:00.130
No, we can't have one of the participants accompany someone.

00:04:00.130 --> 00:04:01.380
But...

00:04:01.690 --> 00:04:05.510
This is a problem, Hino's supposed to go first.

00:04:05.730 --> 00:04:07.640
No, I'll do it.

00:04:08.740 --> 00:04:10.730
Please let me do it.

00:04:14.660 --> 00:04:16.190
Shoji-san?

00:04:16.910 --> 00:04:19.730
That is, if you'll have me.

00:04:22.740 --> 00:04:26.520
I might not have any right to do it.

00:04:27.000 --> 00:04:30.700
But I did something terrible during the first selection.

00:04:31.030 --> 00:04:34.700
I just don't want you to participate.

00:04:35.870 --> 00:04:38.710
I've regretted it every day since then.

00:04:38.710 --> 00:04:42.260
I even thought I should quit playing the piano.

00:04:42.730 --> 00:04:48.370
But when I heard you practicing recently, I remembered.

00:04:48.770 --> 00:04:54.730
Back when I just started, back when playing the piano was just fun.

00:04:55.010 --> 00:04:57.370
I love music.

00:04:57.370 --> 00:05:01.280
So I want to face music straight on, once again!

00:05:03.150 --> 00:05:08.320
So, please! Let me accompany you!

00:05:11.680 --> 00:05:15.040
Thank you, Shoji-san. I'll be happy to have you accompany me.

00:05:15.980 --> 00:05:17.420
Hino-sempai.

00:05:18.430 --> 00:05:20.250
Thank you very much!

00:05:21.170 --> 00:05:22.620
Shoji-san.

00:05:25.670 --> 00:05:28.920
But performing without practicing?

00:05:28.920 --> 00:05:32.500
In that case, Kanayan, why don't we change the performance order?

00:05:32.500 --> 00:05:37.310
If Kaho-chan goes last, then she'll be able to practice a little bit.

00:05:37.580 --> 00:05:40.660
But I don't want to cause anyone any trouble.

00:05:40.660 --> 00:05:42.230
I don't mind.

00:05:45.530 --> 00:05:46.900
Neither do I.

00:05:47.470 --> 00:05:48.570
Nor I.

00:05:48.830 --> 00:05:50.190
But...

00:05:50.190 --> 00:05:52.650
I'm OK with it, too.

00:05:52.650 --> 00:05:53.910
Fuyuumi-chan...

00:05:55.230 --> 00:05:59.610
After coming back out of the blue I have no right to complain.

00:05:59.610 --> 00:06:04.760
Speaking of which, didn't you not have much time to practice either?

00:06:04.990 --> 00:06:09.220
I prepared before my trip to England, so it shouldn't be a problem.

00:06:10.090 --> 00:06:13.310
OK, I'll inform the judges.

00:06:16.120 --> 00:06:19.190
There has been a change in the performance order.

00:06:19.920 --> 00:06:25.360
Performer 1, from the Music Department, class 3-B, Azuma Yunoki-kun.

00:06:25.630 --> 00:06:27.780
Yunoki-sama! I'm so glad!

00:06:28.870 --> 00:06:31.490
Yunoki-sama will be the very first one!

00:06:31.490 --> 00:06:33.470
Yunoki-sama!

00:06:33.470 --> 00:06:36.600
He will be playing "Vocalise," by Rachmaninov.

00:06:50.430 --> 00:06:53.230
It's definitely difficult to say I've prepared fully.

00:06:53.230 --> 00:06:57.440
But having a handicap like this peaks my interest.

00:07:14.030 --> 00:07:17.950
It's a superb performance as always, but his tone seems to have deepened.

00:07:35.130 --> 00:07:39.140
I was really glad that Yunoki-sempai came back.

00:07:39.700 --> 00:07:42.310
You're annoying.

00:07:43.600 --> 00:07:47.700
I was shocked to find out what he was really like,

00:07:47.700 --> 00:07:53.340
but because of that I was able to face everyone who I deceived for so long.

00:07:54.070 --> 00:07:57.990
That I was able to come to grips with what my true feelings were.

00:08:01.090 --> 00:08:05.960
It's not just a delicate sound, it also has this resoluteness to it.

00:08:22.650 --> 00:08:24.810
Yunoki-sama!

00:08:28.050 --> 00:08:30.820
Yunoki! You really moved me!

00:08:30.820 --> 00:08:36.720
I'm not sure I can put it into words, but it's just like you're really back, you know?

00:08:36.720 --> 00:08:39.490
I'm so glad we could perform together!

00:08:40.680 --> 00:08:43.100
Thank you, Hihara.

00:08:43.100 --> 00:08:48.540
Performer 2, from the Music Department, class 3-B, Kazuki Hihara-kun.

00:08:49.220 --> 00:08:53.380
He will be playing "Jupiter" from Holst's "The Planets."

00:08:54.650 --> 00:08:59.710
Kaho-chan, you can do it! I'm going to do my best, because I love playing the trumpet!

00:09:05.800 --> 00:09:10.310
This song goes out to all the people that I love.

00:09:12.260 --> 00:09:18.280
I want my music to cheer up the people I love, to give them courage!

00:09:20.540 --> 00:09:25.330
The first person to teach me how fun music could be was Hihara-sempai.

00:09:26.010 --> 00:09:28.130
You've got to have more fun!

00:09:29.060 --> 00:09:33.300
I wonder how much strength I've gotten from him up until now...

00:09:33.300 --> 00:09:35.880
I want to give a performance that gives back all the support he's given me.

00:09:36.890 --> 00:09:41.350
Thank you for always being there for me, Hihara-sempai.

00:09:51.800 --> 00:09:57.150
It's not just a strong performance. It feels like it's wrapped in a gentle warmth.

00:10:15.830 --> 00:10:18.510
So? Sounds like you played your heart out out there.

00:10:18.770 --> 00:10:23.760
Yeah! While I was playing I could hear my sound just expanding outwards!

00:10:23.760 --> 00:10:27.230
I didn't think I would be able to give a performance like that!

00:10:27.580 --> 00:10:30.380
It was a really wonderful performance.

00:10:30.380 --> 00:10:32.220
Thank you very much!

00:10:32.220 --> 00:10:35.680
I'm loving the trumpet even more now!

00:10:36.610 --> 00:10:42.290
Performer 3, from the Music Department, class 1-B, Shoko Fuyuumi-san.

00:10:42.530 --> 00:10:45.490
She will be playing a Polish folk tune, "Clarinet Polka."

00:11:00.440 --> 00:11:06.180
Fuyuumi-chan... You can perform without being nervous anymore, I see.

00:11:06.620 --> 00:11:09.570
I want to be like you, Kaho-sempai.

00:11:09.570 --> 00:11:13.190
I thought of Fuyuumi-chan like a little sister,

00:11:13.190 --> 00:11:15.570
but you are shining really brightly now.

00:11:15.570 --> 00:11:20.280
Through this competition you've become a splendid young woman.

00:11:23.720 --> 00:11:25.610
She's got a really light touch.

00:11:25.610 --> 00:11:27.450
It's like she's grown wings.

00:11:27.720 --> 00:11:31.830
And it's combined with an impressive display of technique.

00:11:41.780 --> 00:11:47.780
Performer 4, from the Music Department, class 1-A, Keiichi Shimizu-kun.

00:11:47.780 --> 00:11:53.150
He will be playing "Prelude" from Bach's First Suite for Unaccompanied Cello.

00:11:53.490 --> 00:11:56.320
Oh? He changed instruments.

00:11:56.320 --> 00:11:57.980
That's a baroque cello, isn't it?

00:12:09.420 --> 00:12:15.150
I see. For Bach, it's only appropriate to use a instrument contemporary to Bach.

00:12:15.150 --> 00:12:16.810
It's so pretty...

00:12:18.710 --> 00:12:22.680
It's not just accurately played... You can hear his own interpretation as well.

00:12:29.750 --> 00:12:33.820
Shimizu-kun taught me many things.

00:12:34.760 --> 00:12:39.190
I need your sound, Sempai.

00:12:39.720 --> 00:12:44.990
I really respect the seriousness to which he approached his music.

00:12:46.280 --> 00:12:51.540
From now on let's both try and expand the score inside our hearts.

00:13:00.070 --> 00:13:01.300
It's almost time.

00:13:01.780 --> 00:13:03.090
OK!

00:13:03.090 --> 00:13:09.380
Performer 5, from the Music Department, class 2-A, Len Tsukimori-kun.

00:13:09.380 --> 00:13:13.350
He will be playing "Caprice No. 24" by Paganini.

00:13:17.140 --> 00:13:19.070
Hino, can you do it?

00:13:20.340 --> 00:13:24.900
We did what we could. All that's left is to go out there and play.

00:13:28.100 --> 00:13:29.460
Tsukimori-kun...

00:13:44.510 --> 00:13:47.640
It reverberates within my chest, pressing against it...

00:13:47.950 --> 00:13:50.850
Your fingers are meant for playing the violin!

00:13:52.160 --> 00:13:57.870
The first person to teach me how beautiful the violin could sound was Tsukimori-kun.

00:13:58.390 --> 00:14:01.530
But it's not just beautiful now.

00:14:01.950 --> 00:14:06.250
I can feel its power to resonate with the heart, and its kindness.

00:14:07.220 --> 00:14:10.170
He said some pretty harsh things to me,

00:14:10.170 --> 00:14:15.400
but I think it's because of Tsukimori-kun's playing shining in my heart that I've come this far.

00:14:24.920 --> 00:14:28.290
The skill and technique shine through his playing.

00:14:28.290 --> 00:14:31.330
It's an extremely high level of performance.

00:14:31.330 --> 00:14:34.430
He's broken through to a new level, hasn't he?

00:14:55.940 --> 00:14:57.840
Did you have enough time to prepare?

00:14:57.840 --> 00:14:59.990
Well, I can't say it'll be perfect.

00:14:59.990 --> 00:15:01.210
I see.

00:15:01.550 --> 00:15:04.610
Just give your own performance. That'll be for the best.

00:15:08.810 --> 00:15:11.010
Take up the challenge, is what he means.

00:15:14.250 --> 00:15:16.560
I'll say it once again. I'm not going to lose.

00:15:17.860 --> 00:15:19.060
It's your turn.

00:15:21.920 --> 00:15:28.280
Performer 6, from General Studies, class 2-5, Ryotaro Tsuchiura-kun.

00:15:28.280 --> 00:15:30.990
He will be playing "La Campanella" by Liszt.

00:15:48.610 --> 00:15:51.430
You're always saving me, you know?

00:15:52.240 --> 00:15:55.850
I guess you could say that you are there as my violinist.

00:15:56.500 --> 00:16:02.730
You were always kind to me, and worried about me, and sometimes even really got angry with me.

00:16:02.730 --> 00:16:06.980
A straightforward and warm performance, just like you, Tsuchiura-kun.

00:16:06.980 --> 00:16:11.610
I think it's only because you were there for me that I was able to work so hard all this time, Tsuchiura-kun.

00:16:16.250 --> 00:16:18.850
How long do you plan on making that face?

00:16:19.080 --> 00:16:22.290
You're a guy, right? Stop brooding over it.

00:16:22.550 --> 00:16:25.090
I've been liberated.

00:16:25.810 --> 00:16:27.670
Thanks to Hino.

00:16:28.680 --> 00:16:33.160
Playing the piano is just fun for me now, that's all there is to it.

00:16:45.900 --> 00:16:49.030
The subtle details come through even for such a difficult piece.

00:17:13.650 --> 00:17:16.630
It was really great, Tsuchiura!

00:17:16.630 --> 00:17:18.120
Thank you very much.

00:17:21.160 --> 00:17:23.100
It was just your kind of performance.

00:17:24.050 --> 00:17:29.100
So you'll just continue on pursuing your own style, yes?

00:17:29.100 --> 00:17:31.630
Right back at you, there.

00:17:32.360 --> 00:17:37.700
Performer 7, from General Studies, class 2-2, Kahoko Hino-san.

00:17:39.050 --> 00:17:41.630
Shoji-san, shall we go?

00:17:41.630 --> 00:17:42.580
Yes.

00:17:43.610 --> 00:17:45.160
Hino-chan, what about your clothes?

00:17:46.120 --> 00:17:50.110
I think just as I am is fine. Just be myself.

00:17:50.110 --> 00:17:52.650
It's just like you, Kaho-chan.

00:17:52.650 --> 00:17:54.570
Hey now, break a leg.

00:17:55.000 --> 00:17:55.870
Right!

00:17:59.880 --> 00:18:03.350
She will be playing "Ave Maria" by Schubert.

00:18:03.560 --> 00:18:05.050
Kaho-chan?

00:18:05.700 --> 00:18:06.890
Hey, her accompanist...

00:18:07.210 --> 00:18:09.440
Hey, she's just wearing her uniform.

00:18:11.800 --> 00:18:13.110
Kahoko Hino.

00:18:15.860 --> 00:18:17.070
At long last.

00:18:17.710 --> 00:18:18.740
Corda.

00:18:19.280 --> 00:18:22.190
With all the bonds that music has given me...

00:18:22.190 --> 00:18:23.930
I give you my thanks.

00:18:42.710 --> 00:18:44.510
So many things happened.

00:18:45.820 --> 00:18:49.810
All the wonderful people I met thanks to this violin.

00:18:50.650 --> 00:18:54.550
And all the wonderful memories I have thanks to music.

00:18:55.280 --> 00:18:58.950
There were tough times, and tearful times...

00:18:59.570 --> 00:19:03.540
But now they are all so very dear to me.

00:19:14.690 --> 00:19:18.650
That's right. I'm in love with the violin.

00:19:19.660 --> 00:19:21.630
I'm in love with music.

00:19:23.160 --> 00:19:27.420
It supports me, and watches over me.

00:19:28.140 --> 00:19:31.910
It cheers me up, and everyone else.

00:19:35.690 --> 00:19:41.410
I dedicate this song to Lili, who introduced me to music.

00:19:42.590 --> 00:19:47.480
Ave Maria. This is my first step.

00:20:04.850 --> 00:20:06.350
Kaho-chan!

00:20:06.350 --> 00:20:07.350
Kaho...

00:20:12.710 --> 00:20:14.150
Bravo!

00:20:17.940 --> 00:20:19.270
Kaho-chan!

00:20:24.290 --> 00:20:28.290
Can you hear it? Everyone is giving us so much applause!

00:20:29.150 --> 00:20:32.860
Thank you for doing your best for me all this time.

00:20:46.220 --> 00:20:47.590
Kahoko Hino.

00:20:49.610 --> 00:20:50.660
Lili?

00:20:50.660 --> 00:20:54.410
Thanks to you, we had a wonderful competition.

00:20:54.410 --> 00:20:56.780
Thank you so much.

00:20:56.780 --> 00:20:59.530
Me, too. Thanks for everything.

00:20:59.530 --> 00:21:04.000
Lili, I'm going to continue playing this violin.

00:21:04.000 --> 00:21:07.870
I'm going to continue playing the music inside of me.

00:21:08.630 --> 00:21:10.850
For ever and ever...

00:21:10.850 --> 00:21:12.120
Kahoko Hino...

00:21:37.680 --> 00:21:39.290
Kaho-sempai.

00:21:42.620 --> 00:21:43.740
Kahoko.

00:21:53.960 --> 00:21:54.970
Kaho.

00:21:59.610 --> 00:22:00.780
Kahoko.

00:22:04.630 --> 00:22:05.940
Kaho-chan.

00:22:26.880 --> 00:22:31.140
And so I took a new step forward.

00:24:05.780 --> 00:24:08.580
I hope we can meet again sometime.
